# Keep the build context small � a stray sub-project or nested node_modules
# turns a 30MB context into hundreds of MB and slows every build.
# A bare `node_modules` matches only the ROOT; the ** form is required.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/dist

.git
.claude
.vercel
docs
coverage

# The pre-watermark image archive. 432 MB of source photography that the app
# never serves — public/ holds the processed copies it actually uses. It was
# costing that much on every single build: docker uploads the whole context to
# the daemon before running a single instruction, and `docker build` had slowed
# to the point of appearing hung.
#
# Keep the archive in git (it is the only copy of the originals) but keep it out
# of the image.
originals

# Test tooling is not needed at runtime.
#
# It used to be excluded for a second reason as well: playwright.config.ts
# imported the shared QA kit from ../ops/qa/, OUTSIDE the build context, so
# leaving it in made the production type-check fail with "Cannot find module
# '../ops/qa/...'". That reason is gone as of 2026-08-09 — the kit is vendored
# at ops/qa/ and tsconfig.json excludes it — but the exclusion stays, because
# none of this belongs in a production image.
#
# ops/ goes too: it holds the vendored QA kit and the health-check scripts, all
# of which run from a checkout or from /usr/local/bin on the host, never from
# inside the container.
tests
playwright.config.*
playwright-report
test-results
ops
*.tsbuildinfo

.env*
!.env.example
npm-debug.log*
*.md

# Screenshot dumps from QA and earlier sessions: 107 MB that was travelling into
# every build context for nothing. Nothing in the image references them.
test-screenshots
screenshots
_pw_shots
